From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000032 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cennac <cennac@163.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 18:20:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] broadcom: keep AP6275P BT_WAKE asserted on AGIBOT

The MB0002 AP6275P controller has controller sleep disabled, but its
Rockchip kernel still uses /proc/bluetooth/sleep/btwrite to control the
host-wake GPIO.  Sending the proc deassert notification after an idle HCI
transaction leaves the controller unable to answer a remote inquiry or page.

Keep the proc assertion in place for this vendor configuration.  The board
does not use controller low-power mode, so there is no benefit in notifying
the kernel of a deassertion and doing so breaks inbound Classic Bluetooth.
---
 include/vnd_rksdk.txt | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/vnd_rksdk.txt b/include/vnd_rksdk.txt
index 7e7f8d0..f7b75e6 100644
--- a/include/vnd_rksdk.txt
+++ b/include/vnd_rksdk.txt
@@ -25,2 +25,2 @@
 PROC_BTWRITE_TIMER_TIMEOUT_MS = 0
-BT_WAKE_VIA_PROC_NOTIFY_DEASSERT = TRUE
+BT_WAKE_VIA_PROC_NOTIFY_DEASSERT = FALSE
-- 
2.53.0
